course: dictionary
lesson: 4330
title: Grumble: complain or rumble
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so read the words around it. «Alice grumbles that they are wasting time» means she is complaining in a low, unhappy voice. Here grumbles is an action word, a verb.
explain: Grumble can also be a noun, a thing you can have. «The teacher heard a grumble from the back row.» The word a before it is a clue that grumble is a noun, meaning a complaint.
explain: Sometimes grumble means a low, rumbling sound, as in «Thunder grumbled» or «My tummy grumbled». Ask yourself: is someone speaking unhappily, or is something making a rumble? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Grumble as a verb means to complain in a low, unhappy voice.
fact: Grumble as a noun means a complaint.
fact: «Grumbled» can also mean made a low rumbling sound, like «Thunder grumbled».
fact: A «grumbling tummy» means your stomach is making noises because you are hungry.
fact: You can grumble about something or grumble at someone, as in «Children grumble about homework».
exercise: «Tank sniffs his hand, grumbles and lies down.» What does grumbles mean here? | *Complains in a low, unhappy voice | Eats his dinner quickly | Runs away fast | Jumps up with joy
exercise: Ella says, «My tummy is grumbling again.» What does this most likely mean? | She is tired of school | *She is hungry | She is cold and wet | She has a cold
exercise: «Thunder grumbled far away.» What does grumbled mean here? | Shouted angrily at the sky | Turned into rain | *Made a low rumbling sound | Stopped suddenly
test: «The early workers were paid what was promised, yet they grumbled.» What does grumbled mean here? | *Complained in a low, unhappy voice | Fell asleep in the field | Ran off to play | Made a low, rumbling sound
test: The word grumble can be a noun. Which sentence uses it as a noun, meaning a complaint? | We grumbled loudly all afternoon | *The teacher heard a grumble from the back row | The thunder will grumble soon | He likes to grumble about the rain
exam: Ravi says, «My tummy grumbled all through the lesson.» What does this most likely mean? | *He was hungry | He was rude to the teacher | He was fast asleep | He had a sore throat
